Rooms vanished from the admin panel when Firebase data was stored in array format. The conversion code expected rooms to have an `id` property, but IDs are stripped during save operations and used as object keys, causing all rooms to be skipped.

## Changes

**Enhanced array-to-object conversion in `admin-room-manager.js`**
- Generate IDs from room names when missing (normalized to kebab-case)
- Fall back to index-based IDs (`room-0`, `room-1`, etc.)
- Handle ID collisions with incremental counter suffixes
- Preserve all room data during conversion

**Before:**
```javascript
data.forEach((room) => {
  if (room && room.id) {  // Fails - id was removed during save
    roomsData[room.id] = room;
  } else {
    skippedCount++;  // All rooms skipped
  }
});
```

**After:**
```javascript
data.forEach((room, index) => {
  let roomId = room.id;
  if (!roomId && room.name) {
    const generatedId = room.name.toLowerCase()
      .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')
      .replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
    roomId = generatedId || `room-${index}`;
  } else if (!roomId) {
    roomId = `room-${index}`;
  }

  // Ensure uniqueness
  let finalRoomId = roomId;
  let counter = 1;
  while (roomsData[finalRoomId]) {
    finalRoomId = `${roomId}-${counter++}`;
  }

  const { id, ...roomDataWithoutId } = room;
  roomsData[finalRoomId] = roomDataWithoutId;
});
```

The fix auto-repairs corrupted data and persists the corrected format back to Firebase.

