When users cancel Google registration after authenticating, they remain signed into Firebase Auth without a profile, creating an inconsistent state requiring manual sign-out or page refresh.

## Changes

- Import `signOut` from `firebase/auth`
- Call `signOut(auth)` in Cancel button handler before resetting form state
- Wrap signOut in try-catch to prevent blocking form reset on error

```typescript
onClick={async () => {
  // Sign out the user to ensure a clean state
  try {
    if (auth.currentUser) {
      await signOut(auth);
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Error signing out:", err);
    // Continue with form reset even if signOut fails
  }
  setShowGoogleForm(false);
  setGoogleUserData(null);
  // ... reset form data
}}
```

