Addresses feedback from #2 to prevent silent Firebase initialization failures when environment variables are undefined at runtime.

**Changes:**
- Validate required Firebase environment variables before initialization
- Separate required vars (apiKey, authDomain, projectId, storageBucket, messagingSenderId, appId) from optional (measurementId)
- Throw explicit error listing missing variables with actionable guidance

**Implementation:**
```javascript
const requiredEnvVars = {
  apiKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY,
  authDomain: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN,
  // ... other required vars
};

const missingVars = Object.entries(requiredEnvVars)
  .filter(([, value]) => !value)
  .map(([key]) => envVarNames[key]);

if (missingVars.length > 0) {
  throw new Error(
    `Missing required Firebase environment variables: ${missingVars.join(', ')}. ` +
    `Please check your .env.local file and ensure all required Firebase configuration values are set.`
  );
}
```

